# Toma = website recap, not a VO script

When writing or changing the jornada Toma (`/toma`, `jornadaTakeAi`, the paper board), read and follow:

`doc/ACCESO_FUTBOL_SCRIPT_GUIDE.md`

Use **Section 4** (website J4 recap) plus **Section 0** with the website exception.

## Apply
- Accents ON in website copy (`análisis`, `Selección`). The no-accent rule is VO/graphics only.
- No em-dashes. Period or comma.
- First-person take (`yo creo` / `honestamente` / `para mí`) in the column.
- At least one verified stat from the dossier (Sportmonks / cable). Never invent scores.
- Cover the **full jornada window**, including Monday. Not "sábado y domingo."
- Spoken clocks only in Toma copy: `lunes a las nueve de la noche`, `Pachuca contra Puebla`. Never `9:06 p.m. (PAC–PUE)`.
- Cover all games in the slate, not only América / Chivas / Cruz Azul.
- Standings: Apertura 2026 corte is **top 8, no Play-In** (product override of the guide's Play-In line).
- Close with a dividing question (binary or A/B/C), not "síguenos."
- Blocklist as standalone hook: Márquez appointment, Almada arrival, Gignac departure, "Atlante regresó."

## Do not apply (VO-only)
- `Preparense que arrancamos`
- Stripping vowel accents
- TikTok runtime / hashtag packaging
